Task: compile a factual track-record and personality profile of Gabriel Attal (Renaissance) using live web search. Use his campaign statements (attalpresident.fr), Renaissance proposals and his record as minister and Prime Minister (2024).

Cover:
1. bio: 3-4 neutral sentences.
2. offices: every elected/appointed office with dates and kind; executive_experience_years = total years in national or local executive roles (minister, PM, mayor, regional/departmental president).
3. legal: every judicial case involving them personally (not their party only, unless they were personally implicated), with precise current status and date. Presumption of innocence: be exact about status. Empty list if none.
4. reversals: documented, significant policy reversals (max 6, most significant first), each with before/after and sources. Only genuine changes of position, not nuance.
5. delivery: main things they actually did/passed in office and a balanced assessment citing sources of different leanings (max 6).
6. traits: leadership/personality traits that are widely attested (e.g. "consensus-seeking", "confrontational", "technocratic") - only those reported by at least two sources of different leanings; list the leanings in source_leans.
7. media_portrayal: one or two sentences each on how left-leaning, right-leaning and neutral outlets typically portray them (this documents bias, it is not a judgement).
8. sources_note: which outlets you relied on and any bias caveat.

Source discipline (mandatory):
- Today is 5 October 2026. Prefer sources from 2025-2026; use older ones (e.g. 2022 programme) only if no newer position exists, and say so in `nuance`.
- Prefer primary sources: official programme, campaign/party site, Assemblée/Sénat/European Parliament roll-call votes (datan.fr, nosdeputes.fr, howtheyvote.eu, assemblee-nationale.fr), the candidate's own interviews.
